From 65bf097b3d48e180c1dc5498cb69308ded4f87a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Masahito S <firelzrd@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 05:55:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] linux6.18.48-bore-6.8.0

Port BORE 6.8.0 from the 6.18.22 base onto 6.18.48.

6.18.48 picked up the EEVDF pick/preempt rework, so two fair.c hunks
needed adapting (both match the upstream BORE 6.8.0 tree for 7.1.5):

 - reweight_entity(): upstream dropped the place_entity() call in favour
   of the exact "se->vruntime = avruntime - se->vlag" restore, which is
   what BORE's curr special case was open-coding.  BORE's changes here
   are now redundant and are dropped; only the non-static declaration
   (needed by bore.c) is kept.

 - do_preempt_weight(): "do_preempt_short = true" became
   "preempt_action = PREEMPT_WAKEUP_SHORT; goto pick;".

The dequeue_entity()/requeue_delayed_entity()/dequeue_task_fair() hunks
keep their 6.18.22 form, as 6.18.48 has not taken the 7.x rework there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019nVap5Gvqdh3nFtmYRSBE1
